Z||000000||jerpro||12-30-2000||09:57 AM||||It is coming from inside the car.<BR>I hit a bump last night and the squeaking started. Every little vibration is making the car squeak like if there was a door not shut properly. It is coming from the passenger side. I have tried pressing stuff with my hand while driving and I can still hear it!!!! GRRRRRR<BR>It is not the sunroof because it still does it when I open it.<BR>ANybody had any wierd squeaking that had no idea where it came from?<BR>THIs is frustrating me a LOT!!!!!!!!!!!!!<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>please help!<P>(sorry, I needed to vent. I hate annoying squeaky things especially when I have no idea where they come from)<BR><p>[This message has been edited by jerpro (edited 12-30-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||12-30-2000||10:36 AM||||I'll bet it's the roof panel. Mine squeaks a little when it's really cold.<P>My guess is that the plastic contracts more than the metal subframe in extreme cold, causing the squeaking.<P>If it goes away when the car has set in the sun or in warmer weather, that's it. Just grin and bear it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||12-30-2000||11:32 AM||||If you get moisture down between the two fiberglass panels covering the roof and it freezes, it will squeak and creak and drive you insane until it melts.  This has happened to me several times, usually after some freezing rain or after I wash my car in sub-freezing temps.  My 84 and 86 did this every winter - the 88 doesn't for some reason.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||12-30-2000||12:13 PM||||There is a TSB about th roof panel comming loose. You have to pull the headliner to tighten all the hardware. using re-entrant locktite would be a good idea to prevent it happening again. (Blue locktite not red.)||||reg||1
